## Context

The author's questions, 2026-09-02: a work exists in several languages. Can
translated pairs judge the retriever? Should the answer dedup renderings from
the top-k and pad? How should it present, with a note that the work also
exists in VN, EN? Three further questions (detect and autotag translations,
create translations, autosplit bilingual records) were severed the same day
as a library-management spinoff outside this workshop: ticket 0574, ruling in
DECISIONS.md.

`DECISIONS.md` carries the brief as an awaiting entry of the same date, one
answer and one recommendation per question, on facts measured on the author's
library (`bench/results/0573-lang-census.txt`, instrument
`verification/probes/lang_census.py`). This is the tracker: it holds the
direction until ruled, then files one child per accepted recommendation and
stays open until they close (tracking-ticket convention).

Short form of the recommendations, the entry is the record:

1. Parallel slice for R29's gate, from the 157 EN+VI twin records, body
   passages only, both directions. Beside the golden slice, never in its place.
2. Collapse renderings of one work into one answer row before the cut to k;
   declared relations only, never a similarity guess.
3. One row per work, matched rendering first, `also in: <lang> (<key>)`
   fields for the others; relevance order, not query-language order.
4. Prerequisite of 1, kept here as the agent's reading (the author may
   strike it): amend D6 to first-with-text *per language* so both renderings
   of a bilingual record are indexed, which needs a per-attachment language
   identifier on the extracted text, stored as derived data. Splitting such
   records is the spinoff's, not this ticket's.

## Relevant files

- `SPEC.md` §2 (new term "rendering"), §3 R24 (dedup clause), R7 and R29,
  "The resolved decisions" D6, §5.2.6 (collapse and row shape), §5.2.8
  (per-language coverage, if adopted).
- `bench/results/0573-lang-census.txt`, `verification/probes/lang_census.py`.
- Tickets 0029 (golden corpus and gates), 0266 (closed, the cross-lingual
  probe this extends), 0037 (closed, R29), 0563 (language robustness in the
  segmenter), 0483 (per-attachment state, where a skip reason lives).

## Children to file once ruled

One per accepted recommendation, each `Blocked-by` its real prerequisite and
never this tracker: (a) per-attachment language id and the D6 amendment;
(b) the parallel slice in 0029's gate; (c) rendering collapse and row shape in
the query path. Collapse (c) acts on declared relations; which declarations
zoteus reads (twin attachments; Related links) is specified with (c), and
writing any of them is the spinoff's.

## Ruling and children

The author ratified all four recommendations on 2026-09-02. The implementation
train is:

- 0587 — detect attachment language and amend D6 to first-with-text per
  language;
- 0588 — add the body-only EN↔VI parallel evaluation slice;
- 0589 — collapse declared renderings and present one row per work.

Questions 4–6's library-management operations remain deferred to 0574; only
question 6's indexing consequence entered this workshop.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The awaiting entry is ruled on, question by question; all four
      recommendations were accepted.
- [x] SPEC.md matches the ruling (term, D6, R24, §5.2.6); its date was already
      2026-09-02.
- [x] Children filed for the accepted recommendations and listed here.
- [ ] All children closed, then the integration review before this closes.
